#: ../../library/http.client.rst:248
msgid "HTTPConnection Objects"
msgstr "Objekty HTTPConnection"

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:250
msgid ":class:`HTTPConnection` instances have the following methods:"
msgstr "Instance :class:`HTTPConnection` mají následující metody:"

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:256
msgid ""
"This will send a request to the server using the HTTP request method "
"*method* and the request URI *url*. The provided *url* must be an absolute "
"path to conform with :rfc:`RFC 2616 §5.1.2 <2616#section-5.1.2>` (unless "
"connecting to an HTTP proxy server or using the ``OPTIONS`` or ``CONNECT`` "
"methods)."
msgstr ""
"Tato metoda odeslá požadavek serveru pomocí metody HTTP požadavku *method* a"
" identifikátoru URI požadavku *url*. Poskytnutá *url* musí být absolutní "
"cesta, aby vyhověla :rfc:`RFC 2616 §5.1.2 <2616#section-5.1.2>` (pokud se "
"nepipojujete k serveru HTTP proxy nebo nepoužíváte metody ``OPTIONS`` nebo "
"``CONNECT``)."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:262
msgid ""
"If *body* is specified, the specified data is sent after the headers are "
"finished.  It may be a :class:`str`, a :term:`bytes-like object`, an open "
":term:`file object`, or an iterable of :class:`bytes`.  If *body* is a "
"string, it is encoded as ISO-8859-1, the default for HTTP.  If it is a "
"bytes-like object, the bytes are sent as is.  If it is a :term:`file "
"object`, the contents of the file is sent; this file object should support "
"at least the ``read()`` method.  If the file object is an instance of "
":class:`io.TextIOBase`, the data returned by the ``read()`` method will be "
"encoded as ISO-8859-1, otherwise the data returned by ``read()`` is sent as "
"is.  If *body* is an iterable, the elements of the iterable are sent as is "
"until the iterable is exhausted."
msgstr ""
"Je-li zadáno *body*, jsou zadaná data odeslána po dokončení hlaviček. Má to "
"být :class:`str`, :term:`bytes-like objekt`, otevřený :term:`objektsouboru`,"
" nebo iterable z :class:`bytes`. Je-li *body* řetězec, je kódován jako "
"ISO-8859-1, výchozí pro HTTP. Je-li to bytes-like objekt, jsou bajty "
"odeslány tak, jak jsou. Je-li to :term:`objektsouboru`, je odeslán obsah "
"souboru; tento objektsouboru by měl podporovat alespoň metodu ``read()``. "
"Je-li objektsouboru instancí :class:`io.TextIOBase`, budou data vrácená "
"metodou ``read()`` kódována jako ISO-8859-1, jinak jsou data vrácená metodou"
" ``read()`` odeslána tak, jak jsou. Je-li *body* iterable, prvky iterable "
"jsou odeslány, jak jsou, dokud není iterable vycerpán."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:274
msgid ""
"The *headers* argument should be a mapping of extra HTTP headers to send "
"with the request. A :rfc:`Host header <2616#section-14.23>` must be provided"
" to conform with :rfc:`RFC 2616 §5.1.2 <2616#section-5.1.2>` (unless "
"connecting to an HTTP proxy server or using the ``OPTIONS`` or ``CONNECT`` "
"methods)."
msgstr ""
"Argument *headers* by měl být mapováním doplňkových hlaviček HTTP k odeslání"
" spolu s požadavkem. Hlavička :rfc:`Host <2616#section-14.23>` musí být "
"poskytnutá, aby vyhověla :rfc:`RFC 2616 §5.1.2 <2616#section-5.1.2>` (pokud "
"se nepipojujete k serveru HTTP proxy nebo nepoužíváte metody ``OPTIONS`` "
"nebo ``CONNECT``)."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:280
msgid ""
"If *headers* contains neither Content-Length nor Transfer-Encoding, but "
"there is a request body, one of those header fields will be added "
"automatically.  If *body* is ``None``, the Content-Length header is set to "
"``0`` for methods that expect a body (``PUT``, ``POST``, and ``PATCH``).  If"
" *body* is a string or a bytes-like object that is not also a :term:`file "
"<file object>`, the Content-Length header is set to its length.  Any other "
"type of *body* (files and iterables in general) will be chunk-encoded, and "
"the Transfer-Encoding header will automatically be set instead of Content-"
"Length."
msgstr ""
"Pokud *headers* neobsahuje ani Content-Length ani Transfer-Encoding, ale je "
"tady tělo požadavku, bude jedno z těchto polí hlavičky přidáno automaticky. "
"Je-li *body* ``None``, je hlavička Content-Length nastavená na ``0`` pro "
"metody, které očekávají tělo (``PUT``, ``POST`` a ``PATCH``). Je-li *body* "
"řetězec nebo bytes-like objekt, který není také :term:`objektsouboru`, je "
"hlavička Content-Length nastavena na jeho délku. Všechny ostatní typy *body*"
" (soubory a iterables obecně) budou kódovány po částech a hlavička Transfer-"
"Encoding bude automaticky nastavena místo Content-Length."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:292
msgid ""
"The *encode_chunked* argument is only relevant if Transfer-Encoding is "
"specified in *headers*.  If *encode_chunked* is ``False``, the "
"HTTPConnection object assumes that all encoding is handled by the calling "
"code.  If it is ``True``, the body will be chunk-encoded."
msgstr ""
"Argument *encode_chunked* je relevantí pouze pokud je Transfer-Encoding "
"zadán v *headers*. Je-li *encode_chunked* ``False``, předpokládá objekt "
"HTTPConnection, že vše kódování zajišťuje volań.ící kód. Je-li to ``True``, "
"bude tělo kódováno po částech."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:297
msgid ""
"For example, to perform a ``GET`` request to "
"``https://docs.python.org/3/``::"
msgstr ""
"Například k provedení požadavku ``GET`` na ``https://docs.python.org/3/``:"

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:299
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> import http.client\n"
">>> host = \"docs.python.org\"\n"
">>> conn = http.client.HTTPSConnection(host)\n"
">>> conn.request(\"GET\", \"/3/\", headers={\"Host\": host})\n"
">>> response = conn.getresponse()\n"
">>> print(response.status, response.reason)\n"
"200 OK"
msgstr ""
">>> import http.client\n"
">>> host = \"docs.python.org\"\n"
">>> conn = http.client.HTTPSConnection(host)\n"
">>> conn.request(\"GET\", \"/3/\", headers={\"Host\": host})\n"
">>> response = conn.getresponse()\n"
">>> print(response.status, response.reason)\n"
"200 OK"

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:308
msgid ""
"Chunked transfer encoding has been added to the HTTP protocol version 1.1.  "
"Unless the HTTP server is known to handle HTTP 1.1, the caller must either "
"specify the Content-Length, or must pass a :class:`str` or bytes-like object"
" that is not also a file as the body representation."
msgstr ""
"Kódování s postupným přenosem bylo přidáno do verze HTTP protokolu 1.1. "
"Pokud není známo, že server zl. HTTP 1.1, musí volávající buď zadat Content-"
"Length, nebo musí předat :class:`str` nebo bytes-like objekt, který není "
"také souborem, jako reprezentaci těla."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:316
msgid ""
"Note that you must have read the whole response or call :meth:`close` if "
":meth:`getresponse` raised an non-:exc:`ConnectionError` exception before "
"you can send a new request to the server."
msgstr ""
"Pozor na to, že musíte procházet celé odpověď nebo volá :meth:`close`, pokud"
" :meth:`getresponse` vyvolala výjimku mimo :exc:`ConnectionError` před tím, "
"než můžete poslat nový požadavek serveru."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:320
msgid "*body* can now be an iterable."
msgstr "*body* může být iterován."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:323
msgid ""
"If neither Content-Length nor Transfer-Encoding are set in *headers*, file "
"and iterable *body* objects are now chunk-encoded. The *encode_chunked* "
"argument was added. No attempt is made to determine the Content-Length for "
"file objects."
msgstr ""
"Pokud není v *headers* nastaven ani Content-Length ani Transfer-Encoding, "
"jsou objekty souborů a iterable *body* nyní kódovány po částech. Byl přidán "
"argument *encode_chunked*. Nepřijíat se pokus o určení Content-Length pro "
"objekty souborů."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:332
msgid ""
"Should be called after a request is sent to get the response from the "
"server. Returns an :class:`HTTPResponse` instance."
msgstr ""
"Mělo by být volyáno po odeslání požadavku, aby se získala odpověď od "
"serveru. Vrátí instanci :class:`HTTPResponse`."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:335
msgid ""
"If a :exc:`ConnectionError` or subclass is raised, the "
":class:`HTTPConnection` object will be ready to reconnect when a new request"
" is sent."
msgstr ""
"Je-li vyvolna :exc:`ConnectionError` nebo její podTřída, bude objekt "
":class:`HTTPConnection` připraven k opětnému připojení, když bude odeslán "
"nový požadavek."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:340
msgid ""
"Note that this does not apply to :exc:`OSError`\\s raised by the underlying "
"socket. Instead the caller is responsible to call :meth:`close` on the "
"existing connection."
msgstr ""
"Pozor na to, že se to netyka :exc:`OSError`\\ s vyvolvanými podléhajcí "
"socket. Místo toho je volávající odpovědný za volání :meth:`close` na "
"stavaním připojení."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:347
msgid ""
"Set the debugging level.  The default debug level is ``0``, meaning no "
"debugging output is printed.  Any value greater than ``0`` will cause all "
"currently defined debug output to be printed to stdout.  The ``debuglevel`` "
"is passed to any new :class:`HTTPResponse` objects that are created."
msgstr ""
"Nastaví úroveň ladění. Výchozí úroveň ladění je ``0``, což znamená, že není "
"vytisknut žádný výstup ladění. Každá hodnota větší než ``0`` způsobí, že "
"všechny sčásně definované výstupyu ladění budou tisknuty na stdout. "
"``debuglevel`` je předána na nové objekty :class:`HTTPResponse`, které jsou "
"vytvąřeny."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:357
msgid ""
"Set the host and the port for HTTP Connect Tunnelling. This allows running "
"the connection through a proxy server."
msgstr ""
"Nastaví hostitele a port pro HTTP Connect Tunnelling. To umožní spustení "
"připojení skrz proxy server."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:360
msgid ""
"The *host* and *port* arguments specify the endpoint of the tunneled "
"connection (i.e. the address included in the CONNECT request, *not* the "
"address of the proxy server)."
msgstr ""
"Argumenty *host* a *port* určují koncový bod tunelového připojení (tj. "
"adresu zahrnutou v požadavku CONNECT, *nikoli* adresu proxy serveru)."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:364
msgid ""
"The *headers* argument should be a mapping of extra HTTP headers to send "
"with the CONNECT request."
msgstr ""
"Argument *headers* by měl být mapováním doplňkových hlaviček HTTP k odeslání"
" spolu s požadavkem CONNECT."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:367
msgid ""
"As HTTP/1.1 is used for HTTP CONNECT tunnelling request, `as per the RFC "
"<https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7231#section-4.3.6>`_, a HTTP "
"``Host:`` header must be provided, matching the authority-form of the "
"request target provided as the destination for the CONNECT request. If a "
"HTTP ``Host:`` header is not provided via the headers argument, one is "
"generated and transmitted automatically."
msgstr ""
"Jakékoliv HTTP/1.1 se používá pro požadavek HTTP CONNECT tunelování, `podle "
"RFC <https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7231#section-4.3.6>`_, musí "
"být poskytnuta hlavička HTTP ``Host:`` odpovïdající autoritární formě cíle "
"požadavku poskytnuté jako destinace pro požadavek CONNECT. Není-li hlavička "
"HTTP ``Host:`` poskytnuta přes argument headers, bude vygenerována a "
"odeslána automaticky."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:374
msgid ""
"For example, to tunnel through a HTTPS proxy server running locally on port "
"8080, we would pass the address of the proxy to the :class:`HTTPSConnection`"
" constructor, and the address of the host that we eventually want to reach "
"to the :meth:`~HTTPConnection.set_tunnel` method::"
msgstr ""
"Například, chceme-li tunelová skrz HTTPS proxy server běžící lokálně na "
"portu 8080, převedli bychom adresu proxy konstruktoru "
":class:`HTTPSConnection` a adresu hostitele, kterého nakonec chceme "
"dosáhnout, na metodu :meth:`~HTTPConnection.set_tunnel`:"

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:379
msgid ""
">>> import http.client\n"
">>> conn = http.client.HTTPSConnection(\"localhost\", 8080)\n"
">>> conn.set_tunnel(\"www.python.org\")\n"
">>> conn.request(\"HEAD\",\"/index.html\")"
msgstr ""
">>> import http.client\n"
">>> conn = http.client.HTTPSConnection(\"localhost\", 8080)\n"
">>> conn.set_tunnel(\"www.python.org\")\n"
">>> conn.request(\"HEAD\",\"/index.html\")"

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:386
msgid ""
"HTTP CONNECT tunnelling requests use protocol HTTP/1.1, upgraded from "
"protocol HTTP/1.0. ``Host:`` HTTP headers are mandatory for HTTP/1.1, so one"
" will be automatically generated and transmitted if not provided in the "
"headers argument."
msgstr ""
"Požadavky HTTP CONNECT tunelování používají protokol HTTP/1.1, inovovaný z "
"protokolu HTTP/1.0. Hlavičky HTTP ``Host:`` jsou povinny pro HTTP/1.1, takže"
" budou automaticky vygenerovány a odeslány, pokud nebudou poskytnuta v "
"argumentu headers."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:395
msgid ""
"Returns a dictionary with the headers of the response received from the "
"proxy server to the CONNECT request."
msgstr ""
"Vrátí slovník s hlavičkami odpovědi přijaté z proxy serveru na požadavek "
"CONNECT."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:398
msgid "If the CONNECT request was not sent, the method returns ``None``."
msgstr "Pokud požadavek CONNECT nebyl odeslán, metoda vrátí ``None``."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:405
msgid ""
"Connect to the server specified when the object was created.  By default, "
"this is called automatically when making a request if the client does not "
"already have a connection."
msgstr ""
"Připoj se k serveru zadanému při vytváření objektu. Ve výchozím nastavení je"
" to voláno automaticky při vytváření požadavku, pokud klient již nemá "
"připojení."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:409
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``http.client.connect`` with "
"arguments ``self``, ``host``, ``port``."
msgstr ""
"Vyvolvá :ref:`auditovaná událost <auditing>` ``http.client.connect`` s "
"argumenty ``self``, ``host``, ``port``."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:414
msgid "Close the connection to the server."
msgstr "Zavři připojení k serveru."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:419
msgid "Buffer size in bytes for sending a file-like message body."
msgstr ""
"Velikost vyrovnávací paměti v bajtech pro odeslání těla zprávy podobné "
"souboru."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:424
msgid ""
"As an alternative to using the :meth:`~HTTPConnection.request` method "
"described above, you can also send your request step by step, by using the "
"four functions below."
msgstr ""
"Jako alternativu k použití metody :meth:`~HTTPConnection.request` popsáné "
"výše můžete také poslat svůj požadavek postupně pomocí čtyř funkcí níže."

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:431
msgid ""
"This should be the first call after the connection to the server has been "
"made. It sends a line to the server consisting of the *method* string, the "
"*url* string, and the HTTP version (``HTTP/1.1``).  To disable automatic "
"sending of ``Host:`` or ``Accept-Encoding:`` headers (for example to accept "
"additional content encodings), specify *skip_host* or *skip_accept_encoding*"
" with non-False values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:441
msgid ""
"Send an :rfc:`822`\\ -style header to the server.  It sends a line to the "
"server consisting of the header, a colon and a space, and the first "
"argument.  If more arguments are given, continuation lines are sent, each "
"consisting of a tab and an argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:449
msgid ""
"Send a blank line to the server, signalling the end of the headers. The "
"optional *message_body* argument can be used to pass a message body "
"associated with the request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:453
msgid ""
"If *encode_chunked* is ``True``, the result of each iteration of "
"*message_body* will be chunk-encoded as specified in :rfc:`7230`, Section "
"3.3.1.  How the data is encoded is dependent on the type of *message_body*."
"  If *message_body* implements the :ref:`buffer interface <bufferobjects>` "
"the encoding will result in a single chunk. If *message_body* is a "
":class:`collections.abc.Iterable`, each iteration of *message_body* will "
"result in a chunk.  If *message_body* is a :term:`file object`, each call to"
" ``.read()`` will result in a chunk. The method automatically signals the "
"end of the chunk-encoded data immediately after *message_body*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:464
msgid ""
"Due to the chunked encoding specification, empty chunks yielded by an "
"iterator body will be ignored by the chunk-encoder. This is to avoid "
"premature termination of the read of the request by the target server due to"
" malformed encoding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:469
msgid "Added chunked encoding support and the *encode_chunked* parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:475
msgid ""
"Send data to the server.  This should be used directly only after the "
":meth:`endheaders` method has been called and before :meth:`getresponse` is "
"called."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:479
msgid ""
"Raises an :ref:`auditing event <auditing>` ``http.client.send`` with "
"arguments ``self``, ``data``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:485
msgid "HTTPResponse Objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:487
msgid ""
"An :class:`HTTPResponse` instance wraps the HTTP response from the server.  "
"It provides access to the request headers and the entity body.  The response"
" is an iterable object and can be used in a with statement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:492
msgid ""
"The :class:`io.BufferedIOBase` interface is now implemented and all of its "
"reader operations are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:499
msgid "Reads and returns the response body, or up to the next *amt* bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:503
msgid ""
"Reads up to the next len(b) bytes of the response body into the buffer *b*. "
"Returns the number of bytes read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:510
msgid ""
"Return the value of the header *name*, or *default* if there is no header "
"matching *name*.  If there is more than one  header with the name *name*, "
"return all of the values joined by ', '.  If *default* is any iterable other"
" than a single string, its elements are similarly returned joined by commas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:517
msgid "Return a list of (header, value) tuples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:521
msgid "Return the ``fileno`` of the underlying socket."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:525
msgid ""
"A :class:`http.client.HTTPMessage` instance containing the response headers."
"  :class:`http.client.HTTPMessage` is a subclass of "
":class:`email.message.Message`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:531
msgid ""
"HTTP protocol version used by server.  10 for HTTP/1.0, 11 for HTTP/1.1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:535
msgid ""
"URL of the resource retrieved, commonly used to determine if a redirect was "
"followed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:539
msgid ""
"Headers of the response in the form of an "
":class:`email.message.EmailMessage` instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:543
msgid "Status code returned by server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:547
msgid "Reason phrase returned by server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:551
msgid ""
"A debugging hook.  If :attr:`debuglevel` is greater than zero, messages will"
" be printed to stdout as the response is read and parsed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/http.client.rst:556
msgid "Is ``True`` if the stream is closed."
msgstr ""

